# PROJECT: CAMPUSCIRCLE — COLLEGE-EXCLUSIVE SOCIAL COMMUNITY APP

## 1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior Android engineer, product designer, backend architect, database designer, and application security engineer. Build a high-quality, modern, mobile-first native Android application named CampusCircle.

Do not create only a UI prototype. Implement real navigation, functional interactions, authentication, persistent database storage, community feeds, posts, comments, voting, search, and appropriate loading, empty, and error states.

Make sensible engineering decisions without repeatedly asking me basic questions. Prioritize a reliable MVP with a clean architecture and an upgrade path to a production application.

## 2. PRODUCT VISION

CampusCircle is a college-exclusive community platform inspired by Reddit, with elements of anonymous discussion platforms and local discovery applications.

Initial target community: students of Government Engineering College, Bharuch (GEC Bharuch), Gujarat, India.

The app should help students:

- Connect with other students from the same college.
- Create and join topic-specific communities.
- Publish posts and participate in threaded discussions.
- Post anonymously when appropriate.
- Share commute information for students travelling between Vadodara, Bharuch, Surat, and other locations.
- Exchange practical advice about trains, routes, delays, and daily up-down travel.
- Discover affordable food, tiffin services, PGs, rooms, libraries, and useful places in Bharuch.
- Help juniors with academics, college life, placements, internships, and practical advice.
- Share events, memes, polls, questions, and campus experiences.
- Communicate safely with other students.

The experience should feel like a real student community, not a generic corporate dashboard or an AI chatbot.

Use CampusCircle as the working name and make branding easy to change later.

